WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.010
English.

2
00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:01.790
Hindi.

3
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.790
Spanish.

4
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:03.690
Russian.

5
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:04.590
Persian.

6
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.530
Irish.

7
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.250
They seem unrelated.

8
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.750
Yet all belong to one family,
the Indo-European family.

9
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.590
Today, almost half of the world's population
speaks a language from this family.

10
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.630
All descend from one ancestral language.

11
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.890
So how did it reach so far?

12
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.250
Did one empire order everyone to speak it?

13
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.250
In this mission, you'll trace languages
from family to branch to dialect,

14
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.250
and find where cultural traits begin.

15
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.170
Then you'll weigh new evidence on
where this family's hearth lay.

16
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.210
Your mission: explain how one ancient
language became the ancestor of so many

17
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.760
of the world's languages.
